{
  "id": "q-tool-go-sdk-ingest",
  "question": "I'm building a Go service to stream Stellar ledger data — what's the official Go SDK and which package handles ingestion?",
  "surface": [
    "stellarDocs.search_protocol_concepts_docs",
    "stellarDocs.search_rpc_horizon_data_docs",
    "stellarDocs.search_sdk_cli_tools_docs"
  ],
  "golden": {
    "answer": "Use SDF's Go module `github.com/stellar/go-stellar-sdk`. For ledger streaming and ingestion, import its `ingest` package to parse raw ledger XDR and `ingest/ledgerbackend` to choose the ledger source, such as Captive Core or a data lake. The old `github.com/stellar/go` repository is archived; do not start new code there.",
    "keyFacts": [
      "The official Go SDK module is `github.com/stellar/go-stellar-sdk`.",
      "Raw ledger ingestion uses `go-stellar-sdk/ingest` with `ingest/ledgerbackend`.",
      "`github.com/stellar/go` is archived and not for new code."
    ],
    "avoid": [
      "Do NOT cite `github.com/stellar/go/ingest` as the current SDK path.",
      "Do NOT pin a go-stellar-sdk release without an as-of date."
    ]
  },
